[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one bug, one fix. Read by tenant, channel and form
instead of by subject line, its reports hold three problems. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 closed on 5 October: parser fixed, booking-v3 form retired. The one-day moves are not fixed.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| problem | what happens | ticket | engineering |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | the shared parser reads every date month first; a day-first tenant books 7 April and the invite says 4 July | [#1](https://github.com/Sepcio88/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `hint` | `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, people type month first, the form reads day first | [#2](https://github.com/Sepcio88/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired |
| one-day move | the date moves by one day instead of flipping; Lisbon and Toronto get different days for one meeting | [#3](https://github.com/Sepcio88/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3) | open |

The counts are the desk's own: the table above, as exported. `hint` is the row marked "not this
ticket": it was merged into #4471 but is a different bug. The one-day moves are the footnote under
`parser`: the desk files them there by tenant, so they are counted in `parser` and have their own
ticket for the time zone bug.

## How to read reports next time

- Group by **tenant, channel and form**, not by subject or intake tag: intake guesses from the
  reporter's browser.
- A report that does not swap day and month is not this bug, whatever its subject says.
- The export repeats rows across pages; count by report id.

